<title>GERMANY: France will stick to EMU plan - de Charette.</title>
<headline>France will stick to EMU plan - de Charette.</headline>
<dateline>BERLIN 1996-10-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>French Foreign Minister Herve de Charette insisted on Monday Paris would stick to the timetable and criteria for Europe's planned single currency as laid down in the Maastricht treaty on European Union.</p>
<p>&quot;We will respect the criteria of the Maastricht treaty, and the timetable which it lays down for the establishment of the single currency will be adhered to,&quot; de Charette told an audience of business and political leaders in Berlin.</p>
<p>The Maastricht treaty calls for would-be members of a single currency to meet a range of financial criteria by 1998 and schedules the final phase of monetary union for 1999.</p>
